Substitution failure inside a concept-id's argument must make the
atomic constraint unsatisfied ([temp.constr.atomic]/3); CBMC keeps
the constrained overload viable and selects it (wrong code).  Root of
the cpp20 *_libcxx failures (same_as inside common_reference_with).
Update 2026-07-24: the atom classification fix handles evaluated
clauses, but THIS test's clause never reaches evaluation: the parser
fails to store a requires-clause whose constraint is a concept
TEMPLATE-ID (rConditionalExpr parses the '<' as less-than, the
post-clause token whitelist then mismatches, and only a constraint
COUNT is kept -- parse.cpp rTempArgList requires-clause fallback).
Fix direction: parse concept template-ids in requires-clauses.
The parse-drop is captured minimally in
cpp20_requires_clause_concept_template_id (multi-argument concept
template-id in a requires-clause).
